===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmæki/|lang=fi}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fiu-pro|fi}} {{term/t|fiu-pro|*mäki}}. Cognates include Estonian {{term|mägi|lang=et}} and Khanty {{term|мӱг|sc=Cyrl|tr=müg|lang=kca}}.

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# A [[hill]] (a relatively large, usually rounded elevation of earth; generally larger than {{term|kukkula||hill, hillock}}, smaller than {{term|vuori||mountain}})
# A [[slope]]

